## 5. Worked example — MehhSpace

### Reference host snapshot (what I verified on Zack's box)

```
node  v22.23.2      npm 10.9.8      git 2.47.3      gh 2.46.0
gh:   logged in as hiimzackjones, scopes [gist, read:org, repo], git protocol ssh
repo: https://github.com/hiimzackjones/hiimzackjones.github.io  (GitHub user site)
push: git push --dry-run origin main  → OK
```

So on this host, the **machine/toolchain/auth layers (checklist rows 1–3) are already
satisfied.** If WebClaude runs here, Push works today with zero setup.

### The three commands and what each needs

| Command | Tools it declares | Extra dependency | Runs headless? |
|---|---|---|---|
| `/MehhSpacePush` | `Bash(git/npm/gh)` | git push auth (have it) | ✅ yes, as-is |
| `/MehhSpaceServe` | `Bash(npm/lsof/kill/curl/ip/hostname/rm)` | a way to *view* :4321 (§4) | ✅ runs; viewing per §4 |
| `/MehhSpaceUpdate` | `Bash(node/npm)`, `Read`, `Write` | **a Notion MCP** (§3) | ⚠️ needs Notion connected |

`/MehhSpaceUpdate` is the only one with a hard MCP dependency. Its flow:
1. Query all `Status = Published` rows from the Notion data source (one SQL-style call).
2. For body-backed tags (`Blog`, `Lab`, `Personal`, `Classes`, `Resume`, `About_Me`)
   the query returns `Content: null` — fetch each page's body/blocks individually and
   take the markdown from the returned content.
3. Hand the rows to the deterministic transform `scripts/mehhspace-update.mjs`, which
   rewrites `src/data/*.json` and `src/content/**/*.md`. (This half is pure local
   `node` + `Write` — no Notion — and is unit-tested via `node scripts/run-tests.mjs`.)

### Notion coordinates for this repo

```
Database title : MehhSpace Content
Page ID (dashed): 7b044117-0f64-44ef-a387-4479b6932b73
Data source ID : cd6f8147-f900-45f2-9f4f-0d3e6a0862b6   (the query target)
Query (verified working):
  SELECT "Name","Tag","Content","Slug","Category","Status","Order",
         "Featured","Image","date:Date:start","File", url
  FROM "collection://cd6f8147-f900-45f2-9f4f-0d3e6a0862b6"
  WHERE "Status" = ?            -- params: ["Published"]
  ORDER BY "Tag" ASC, "Order" ASC
```

### Mapping the command onto WebClaude's Notion connector

If you have `mcp__claude_ai_Notion__*` instead of `plugin:Notion:notion`:
- **Step 1 query** → use the data-source query tool (`notion-query-data-sources` or
  equivalent) against data source `cd6f8147-…`. If it doesn't accept the exact SQL,
  reproduce the semantics: filter `Status = Published`, sort by `Tag` then `Order`.
- **Step 2 body fetch** → use the page-fetch tool (`notion-fetch` or equivalent) on
  each body-backed row's page id/url; take the markdown from the returned content.
- Everything downstream (the transform, the writes, the build, the push) is identical
  and host-local.

### MehhSpace parity checklist (do these and it fully works from WebClaude)

- [ ] WebClaude's Bash/Read/Write run on the box holding this repo (or a clone with
      deps installed + push auth).
- [ ] WebClaude loads `.claude/commands/*.md` and exposes the three slash-commands.
- [ ] A Notion MCP is connected + authorized for Zack's workspace (§3).
- [ ] Either the command uses `plugin:Notion:notion`, or you've mapped it to your
      Notion connector's query + fetch tools (above).
- [ ] A viewing path for `:4321` exists, or Serve is treated as optional (§4).
- [ ] Sanity: `node scripts/run-tests.mjs` passes; `npm run build` is green.

